/**
\defgroup basis_bspline B-spline bases
\brief Complete B-spline basis with analytical derivatives to order 6, integrals from the lower boundary, and cross Gram matrices.

This module implements univariate B-spline bases of degree \f$d \le 10\f$ in `<laplace/basis/bspline.hpp>`. Users construct a \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner "bspline_basis_owner" on the host and call \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::host "host()" or \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::device "device()" to obtain a lightweight \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis "bspline_basis" view. Evaluation members are marked `LAPLACE_HD` for host code and Kokkos device kernels; constructors, cross Gram matrices, Greville abscissae, and regularity points run on the host. Across 42 knot configurations, rows of orders 0 to 6 stay within 7 ulp for \f$d \le 5\f$ and 19 ulp for \f$d = 10\f$, integrals and column totals within 3 and 4.7 ulp, and cross Gram matrices within 6 ulp against exact rational references.

## Mathematical definition

A B-spline basis of degree \f$d\f$ (\f$0 \le d \le 10\f$, \ref laplace::basis::bspline_max_degree "bspline_max_degree") and dimension \f$K \ge d + 1\f$ is defined by a non-decreasing knot vector \f$t_0 \le t_1 \le \dots \le t_{K+d}\f$ of \f$K + d + 1\f$ real knots. The domain is \f$[t_d, t_K]\f$ (\ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::lower "lower" and \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::upper "upper"), where the \f$K\f$ basis functions \f$B_0(x), \dots, B_{K-1}(x)\f$ satisfy \f$\sum_{j=0}^{K-1} B_j(x) = 1\f$.

For \f$x \in [t_d, t_K]\f$, let \f$s \in [d, K - 1]\f$ be the interval with \f$t_s \le x < t_{s+1}\f$, assigning \f$x = t_K\f$ to \f$s = K - 1\f$. With \f$B_{i, 0}(x) = 1\f$ for \f$i = s\f$ and \f$0\f$ otherwise, the Cox-de Boor recursion for \f$p = 1, \dots, d\f$ is:
\f[
B_{i, p}(x) = \frac{x - t_i}{t_{i+p} - t_i} B_{i, p-1}(x) + \frac{t_{i+p+1} - x}{t_{i+p+1} - t_{i+1}} B_{i+1, p-1}(x)
\f]
treating terms with vanishing denominators as zero, and setting \f$B_j(x) = B_{j, d}(x)\f$ for \f$j = 0, \dots, K - 1\f$.

### Knot multiplicity and row representation

A knot value may appear at most \f$d + 1\f$ times. At an interior knot of multiplicity \f$\mu\f$, continuity is \f$c = d - \mu\f$: multiplicity \f$\mu = 1\f$ gives \f$C^{d-1}\f$ continuity, \f$\mu = d\f$ gives \f$C^0\f$ continuity with discontinuous first derivative, and \f$\mu = d + 1\f$ gives a \f$C^{-1}\f$ jump.

At any \f$x \in [t_d, t_K]\f$, at most \f$w = d + 1\f$ functions \f$B_{s-d, d}(x), \dots, B_{s, d}(x)\f$ are non-zero. Following the row representation of \ref basis, evaluation writes \f$w\f$ values (`row_width()`) and returns the first active column \f$f = s - d\f$.

## Domain and special values

The basis is right-continuous on \f$[t_d, t_K]\f$ with left limits at \f$t_K\f$. Outside \f$[t_d, t_K]\f$, evaluation follows \ref laplace::basis::outside_domain_rule "outside_domain_rule" (default `outside_domain_rule::linear`), whose rules and \f$10^{-8}\f$ width tolerance for `outside_domain_rule::nan` are defined on \ref basis.

Derivatives of order \f$k > d\f$ are identically zero. If \f$x\f$ is NaN, row and integral evaluation write quiet NaN and return 0, and expansions return quiet NaN; expansions also return quiet NaN if any active coefficient \f$\beta_j\f$ is NaN.

## Method

Knot allocation stays on the host while lightweight views evaluate all quantities without caller scratch memory (`scratch_size()` is 0).

### Construction and storage

The owner \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner "bspline_basis_owner" stores the \f$K + d + 1\f$ knots in host `std::vector<double>` and device `Kokkos::View<double*, device_memory>`. Calling `owner.host()` or `owner.device()` returns a \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis "bspline_basis" pointing to host or device memory; deleted `const&&` overloads disallow temporary owners.

Four static constructors build knot vectors:
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::uniform_clamped "uniform_clamped()" spaces interior knots by \f$h = (t_K - t_d)/(K - d)\f$ and repeats \f$t_d\f$ and \f$t_K\f$ each \f$d + 1\f$ times.
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::uniform_extended "uniform_extended()" places all knots at step \f$h = (t_K - t_d)/(K - d)\f$, extending \f$d\f$ steps past each end (\f$t_j = t_d + (j - d)h\f$ for \f$j < K\f$, \f$t_j = t_K + (j - K)h\f$ for \f$j \ge K\f$, Eilers and Marx) so every function translates one cardinal B-spline.
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::clamped "clamped()" takes non-decreasing interior knots in \f$(t_d, t_K)\f$ and repeats each endpoint \f$d + 1\f$ times.
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::from_knots "from_knots()" accepts a complete non-decreasing knot vector \f$t_0, \dots, t_{K+d}\f$.

The host function \ref laplace::basis::quantile_knots "quantile_knots(x, m)" places \f$m\f$ strictly increasing interior knots at sample quantiles \f$j / (m + 1)\f$ (\f$j = 1, \dots, m\f$) via R's type-7 linear interpolation between sorted order statistics.

### Interval search

For uniform knots (`step` \f$h > 0\f$), \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::interval "interval()" computes \f$s = d + \lfloor (x - t_d)/h \rfloor\f$ clamped to \f$[d, K - 1]\f$ and checks \f$t_s\f$ and \f$t_{s+1}\f$ to correct rounding near knots. When `step == 0`, it uses binary search for the largest \f$s \in [d, K - 1]\f$ with \f$t_s \le x\f$.

### Values and derivatives

Active values \f$B_{s-d, d}(x), \dots, B_{s, d}(x)\f$ are computed by de Boor's BSPLVB recurrence from degree \f$0\f$ to \f$d\f$. Derivative orders \f$k \in \{1, \dots, 6\}\f$ run BSPLVB to degree \f$d - k\f$ followed by \f$k\f$ steps of:
\f[
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x} B_{i, p}(x) = p \left( \frac{B_{i, p-1}(x)}{t_{i+p} - t_i} - \frac{B_{i+1, p-1}(x)}{t_{i+p+1} - t_{i+1}} \right)
\f]
treating vanishing denominators as zero. Expansions \f$\sum_{j=0}^{K-1} \beta_j B_j^{(k)}(x)\f$ take the inner product of active coefficients with the evaluated row.

### Integral from the lower boundary

The member \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::integral_row "integral_row()" evaluates \f$\int_{t_d}^x B_j(t) \, \mathrm{d}t\f$ on \f$j = s - d, \dots, s\f$ from degree-\f$(d + 1)\f$ B-splines:
\f[
\int_{t_j}^x B_{j, d}(t) \, \mathrm{d}t = \frac{t_{j+d+1} - t_j}{d + 1} \sum_{i=j}^s B_{i, d+1}(x) - \int_{t_j}^{t_d} B_{j, d}(t) \, \mathrm{d}t
\f]
where the subtracted term is non-zero only when knots lie below \f$t_d\f$. Preceding columns \f$j < s - d\f$ equal \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::integral_column_total "integral_column_total()" (\f$\int_{t_d}^{t_K} B_j(t) \, \mathrm{d}t\f$), and succeeding columns \f$j > s\f$ are zero; \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::integral_expansion "integral_expansion()" accumulates both directly.

### Cross Gram matrices, Greville abscissae, and regularity points

The host member \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::cross_gram "cross_gram()" evaluates \f$(G_{kl})_{ij} = \int_{t_d}^{t_K} B_i^{(k)}(x) B_j^{(l)}(x) \, \mathrm{d}x\f$ in dense \f$K \times K\f$ column-major order (`out[i + j * K]`) with semi-bandwidth \f$d\f$ (`gram_bandwidth()`), returning zero if \f$k > d\f$ or \f$l > d\f$. It applies 16-node Gauss-Legendre quadrature (exact to degree 31, covering \f$2d \le 20\f$) on each interval \f$[t_s, t_{s+1}]\f$ in local coordinates \f$u = x - t_s\f$.

The host member \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::greville "greville()" computes \f$\xi_j = \frac{1}{d} \sum_{i=1}^d t_{j+i}\f$ for \f$d \ge 1\f$ (satisfying \f$\sum_{j=0}^{K-1} \xi_j B_j(x) = x\f$) and \f$(t_j + t_{j+1})/2\f$ for \f$d = 0\f$. The host member \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::regularity_points "regularity_points()" returns distinct interior knots with continuity \f$c = d - \mu\f$, plus \f$t_d\f$ and \f$t_K\f$ with continuity \f$1\f$ when `outside` is `outside_domain_rule::linear` and \f$d \ge 2\f$.

## Accuracy

See \ref accuracy "How accuracy is measured" for error definitions and reference generation. Rational references (`fractions.Fraction`, `tools/reference/basis_bspline.py`), confirmed with SymPy (`bspline_basis_set`), cover 42 configurations for \f$d \in \{0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 10\}\f$ (uniform clamped and extended, random knots, multiplicities \f$2, \dots, d + 1\f$, width \f$10^{-12}\f$, and \f$[1000, 1001]\f$) at random points, knots, and points one ulp away.

Row errors are measured in ulp of the row's largest value, integrals and totals in ulp of the largest total, and Gram entries in ulp of the largest entry. The same maxima and test bounds (`tests/basis/test_bspline.cpp`) hold on gcc/OpenMP and CUDA (RTX 4070 SUPER):

| Quantity | Max error (\f$d \le 5\f$) | Bound (\f$d \le 5\f$) | Max error (\f$d = 10\f$) | Bound (\f$d = 10\f$) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Rows, orders 0 to 6 | 7 ulp | 12.0 ulp | 19 ulp | 32.0 ulp |
| Integrals and column totals | 3 ulp | 8.0 ulp | 4.7 ulp | 12.0 ulp |
| Cross Gram matrices | 6 ulp | 12.0 ulp | 6 ulp | 12.0 ulp |

See `docs/numerics.md` for per-case logs and design measurements.

## Speed

Measured in `benchmarks/basis_bspline.cpp` for cubic uniform clamped B-splines (\f$d = 3\f$) on \f$[0, 1]\f$ at \f$n = 10^6\f$ points against R 4.6.0 `splines2` 0.5.4 (`splines2::bSpline`) and `splines` (`splines::splineDesign`), which allocate a dense \f$n \times K\f$ matrix per call. Timings cover one gcc thread, 16 OpenMP threads, and CUDA (RTX 4070 SUPER):

| Evaluation mode (\f$n = 10^6\f$, values) | \f$K = 10\f$ | \f$K = 40\f$ |
|---|---|---|
| `splines2::bSpline` | 107 ms | 412 ms |
| `splines::splineDesign` | 141 ms | 216 ms |
| Laplace dense, one thread | 22.2 ms | 20.7 ms |
| Laplace sparse, one thread | 18.8 ms | 15.8 ms |
| Laplace sparse, 16 threads | 2.7 ms | 2.7 ms |
| Laplace dense, CUDA | 0.38 ms | 2.0 ms |
| Laplace sparse, CUDA | 0.37 ms | 0.37 ms |

Second derivatives and integrals cost 1.1 to 2.0 times the values. Sparse rows keep cost independent of \f$K\f$, whereas dense output is limited by writing zeros, particularly on CUDA.

## Example

This example constructs a cubic uniform clamped basis and evaluates values and second derivatives in a `Kokkos::parallel_for` kernel:

\code{.cpp}
#include <laplace/basis/bspline.hpp>
#include <Kokkos_Core.hpp>

void eval_bspline(const Kokkos::View<const double*>& x,
                  Kokkos::View<int*>& first_col,
                  Kokkos::View<double**, Kokkos::LayoutRight>& val,
                  Kokkos::View<double**, Kokkos::LayoutRight>& d2,
                  int n) {
  constexpr int dim = 8;
  constexpr int degree = 3;
  constexpr int w = degree + 1;

  const auto owner = laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::uniform_clamped(
      0.0, 1.0, dim, degree);
  const laplace::basis::bspline_basis basis = owner.device();

  Kokkos::parallel_for("eval_bspline", n, KOKKOS_LAMBDA(const int i) {
    double row_val[w];
    double row_d2[w];
    const int f = basis.row(x(i), row_val);
    basis.row_d2(x(i), row_d2);
    first_col(i) = f;
    for (int q = 0; q < w; ++q) {
      val(i, q) = row_val[q];
      d2(i, q) = row_d2[q];
    }
  });
}
\endcode

## Module functions and types

### Types and constants

- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_max_degree "bspline_max_degree" — Maximum degree (\f$d_{\max} = 10\f$)
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_regularity_point "bspline_regularity_point" — Reduced-continuity point \f$C^c\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis "bspline_basis" — Lightweight evaluation view
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner "bspline_basis_owner" — Host and device knot owner

### Member functions of bspline basis

- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::dimension "dimension()" — Basis dimension \f$K\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::row_width "row_width()" — Active row width \f$w = d + 1\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::scratch_size "scratch_size()" — Caller scratch size (0)
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::gram_bandwidth "gram_bandwidth()" — Cross Gram semi-bandwidth \f$d\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::row "row()" — Basis row, order 0
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::row_d1 "row_d1()" — First-derivative row
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::row_d2 "row_d2()" — Second-derivative row
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::row_d3 "row_d3()" — Third-derivative row
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::row_d4 "row_d4()" — Fourth-derivative row
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::row_d5 "row_d5()" — Fifth-derivative row
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::row_d6 "row_d6()" — Sixth-derivative row
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::expansion "expansion()" — Linear expansion \f$\sum \beta_j B_j(x)\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::expansion_d1 "expansion_d1()" — First-derivative expansion
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::expansion_d2 "expansion_d2()" — Second-derivative expansion
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::expansion_d3 "expansion_d3()" — Third-derivative expansion
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::expansion_d4 "expansion_d4()" — Fourth-derivative expansion
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::expansion_d5 "expansion_d5()" — Fifth-derivative expansion
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::expansion_d6 "expansion_d6()" — Sixth-derivative expansion
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::integral_row "integral_row()" — Active window of integrals from \f$t_d\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::integral_column_total "integral_column_total()" — Full-domain column integral
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::integral_expansion "integral_expansion()" — Integrated expansion from \f$t_d\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::interval "interval()" — Knot interval index \f$s\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::cross_gram "cross_gram()" — Cross Gram matrix \f$G_{kl}\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::greville "greville()" — Greville abscissae
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::regularity_points "regularity_points()" — Reduced-continuity points

### Data members of bspline basis

- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::knots "knots" — Pointer to knot vector
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::degree "degree" — Polynomial degree \f$d\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::dim "dim" — Total number of basis functions \f$K\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::lower "lower" — Lower domain boundary \f$t_d\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::upper "upper" — Upper domain boundary \f$t_K\f$
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::step "step" — Uniform knot step \f$h > 0\f$ (0 otherwise)
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis::outside "outside" — Outside-domain rule

### Member functions of bspline basis owner

- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::uniform_clamped "bspline_basis_owner::uniform_clamped()" — Uniform clamped constructor
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::uniform_extended "bspline_basis_owner::uniform_extended()" — Uniform extended constructor
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::clamped "bspline_basis_owner::clamped()" — Clamped interior-knots constructor
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::from_knots "bspline_basis_owner::from_knots()" — Full knot-vector constructor
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::host "host()" — Host evaluation view
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::device "device()" — Device evaluation view
- \ref laplace::basis::bspline_basis_owner::knots "knots()" — Host knot vector reference

### Standalone functions

- \ref laplace::basis::quantile_knots "quantile_knots()" — Sample-quantile interior knots (R type 7)
*/
